helen: FYI legal signed off on the websocket endpoint changes. v1 ws API will be removed in 45 days. We need a migration note showing the new subprotocol, auth method, and reconnect behavior. I drafted a PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/14567

diego: Thanks. Key changes to call out: subprotocol changed from `rw.v1` -> `rw.v2.stream`, auth moved from query param `?key=` to `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol: rw-auth=<token>`, and v2 uses framed events for partial outputs. Add examples for both wscat and a Node ws client.

ashley: Also call out the heartbeat/ping behavior: v2 expects clients to send a ping every 30s or server will close idle connections. Include sample reconnection backoff recommended (jittered exponential, cap 60s).

ops-bot: New draft PR opened by helen: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/14567  title: "ws: v1->v2 subprotocol + auth migration"  CI queued.

docs-bot: Please include a short troubleshooting section: signature mismatch, token expiry, and partial-frame reassembly. Also add a smoke-test checklist for infra: staging ws echo, framed-order test, reconnect flakiness.

helen: Draft wscat example for PR:
```bash
# legacy (v1) wscat
wscat -c "wss://api.redwood.ai/v1/stream?key=$RW_KEY"
# v2 (new): pass token in Sec-WebSocket-Protocol
wscat -H "Sec-WebSocket-Protocol: rw-auth=$RW_KEY, rw.v2.stream" -c "wss://api.redwood.ai/v2/stream"
```

diego: Nice. Add node example showing reconnection and frame assembly (paste into PR):
```js
// node ws client (frameless -> now framed events)
import WebSocket from 'ws';
function connect() {
  const ws = new WebSocket('wss://api.redwood.ai/v2/stream', {
    headers: { 'Sec-WebSocket-Protocol': `rw-auth=${process.env.RW_KEY}, rw.v2.stream` }
  });
  ws.on('open', () => console.log('open'));
  ws.on('message', (data) => {
    // data is a framed JSON event, may be partial
    try {
      const evt = JSON.parse(data.toString());
      if (evt.type === 'frame') process.stdout.write(evt.payload || '');
      if (evt.type === 'end') console.log('\n<end>');
    } catch (e) { console.error('parse error', e); }
  });
  ws.on('close', (code) => {
    console.log('closed', code);
    // reconnect with backoff
    setTimeout(connect, 500 + Math.random()*1000);
  });
}
connect();
```

